WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.899
The sacrifices that you've made over the
years, I'm not actually sure if I can

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.600
repay you for. I'm getting upset now...

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.240
Dear mum, I love that you can spell every single word

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.800
in the dictionary when I
need to WhatsApp you and ask you how to

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.740
compose emails and letters. Dear mum,
from watching you you have taught me how

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:29.970
to be a badass... When I needed you, you
dropped everything. Your work, your social

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:35.579
life, your own relationships to be by my
side in a difficult time not only

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:40.800
difficult for me but for you and dad. You
raised me pretty much on your own and I

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.660
can't imagine that to be very easy.
You've taught me acceptance and not to

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.370
strive to be somebody else or search for
change in unchangeable situations. You

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.809
always made sure your kids always had,
even if it meant that you would go

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:59.070
without and the sacrifices that you've
made over the years I'm not actually

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:04.589
sure if I can repay you for even if I
tried. When I was single and alone you

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:07.380
were a best friend to me but more
importantly you were the ultimate

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.799
hospital buddy,
staying every night with me before surgery,

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:15.270
sitting with me in recovery. Sometimes I
was boring, sometimes I was depressed,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:18.479
sometimes I just had nothing to talk
about because I didn't do anything with my

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:22.320
life but you were always there to watch
daytime telly with me and help me heal

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.549
from the inside and out.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:39.159
Having to leave my daughter at hospital
after she came early literally broke my

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:43.780
heart in two. I blamed myself because I'm
a petite woman I kind of thought my body

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.799
just couldn't handle pregnancy and that
maybe I just wasn't ever meant to be

00:01:47.799 --> 00:02:01.630
a mum. 
I blamed myself more so just because of

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.950
like the job that I do, like, social media
and people would make me feel like it

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.860
was my own fault.
People would say things to me like I'll

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.000
be surprised if your baby survives
because your bump is so small and then

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.640
it would scare me and I really think
that my baby wouldn't make it, but it's fine, had mum.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.489
I had you back Jayde, don't you worry. When
you said about you know the hours we

00:02:24.489 --> 00:02:28.810
spent in hospital together, we always
tried to find the funny side of things

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.620
didn't we? We always try to make light of
what was happening because it helped

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.220
helped us both. I'm so proud of how far
you've come. Thank you.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:42.020
You know you're not a selfish
person you know you give what you can

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:48.600
Aww, don't get upset. You're good
to me, you look after me I'm just

00:02:48.609 --> 00:02:54.130
grateful, you'll be the daughter that
you are. You've grown so much in yourself

00:02:54.130 --> 00:03:01.060
and I'm just so immensely proud of you.
Just keep doing what you're doing Jayde

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:06.810
and you will get far, don't bother with
people, what they got to say just

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.830
just do you.

